[{:db/id "71941b2e-6492-57b3-9f15-2ea08ef07538" :answer/id #uuid "71941b2e-6492-57b3-9f15-2ea08ef07538" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "98de73de-134d-534b-abc3-ac5f77866e97" :answer/id #uuid "98de73de-134d-534b-abc3-ac5f77866e97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ae9a6ca6-8dbd-553d-aac4-d168e560858b" :answer/id #uuid "ae9a6ca6-8dbd-553d-aac4-d168e560858b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c20e4615-a0de-539b-8d9d-86666c3a6a40" :answer/id #uuid "c20e4615-a0de-539b-8d9d-86666c3a6a40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a1f39197-e7b1-5769-b28c-870aa6abc063" :answer/id #uuid "a1f39197-e7b1-5769-b28c-870aa6abc063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2ca3c765-a8cc-5f28-93ee-3d5fd340c30b" :answer-field/id #uuid "2ca3c765-a8cc-5f28-93ee-3d5fd340c30b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["71941b2e-6492-57b3-9f15-2ea08ef07538" "98de73de-134d-534b-abc3-ac5f77866e97" "ae9a6ca6-8dbd-553d-aac4-d168e560858b" "c20e4615-a0de-539b-8d9d-86666c3a6a40" "a1f39197-e7b1-5769-b28c-870aa6abc063"] :answer-field/correct "71941b2e-6492-57b3-9f15-2ea08ef07538" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "b21cce72-05b1-50b1-986f-ae9d83039518" :question/id #uuid "b21cce72-05b1-50b1-986f-ae9d83039518" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=\\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\ln{\\left(x - y \\right)}\\right)\\,j.$ \nEvaluate $\\nabla\\cdot F$ at the point $(3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=\\nabla\\cdot F=\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nWhen differentiating $P$ with respect to $x$, hold $y$ constant; when differentiating $Q$ with respect to $y$, hold $x$ constant.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\cdot F & =\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)})+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(3 \\ln{\\left(x - y \\right)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x + y}+\\left(- \\frac{3}{x - y}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{x + 5 y}{\\left(x - y\\right) \\left(x + y\\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(3,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\nabla\\cdot F)(3,1) & =- \\frac{5 (1) + (3)}{\\left(- (1) + (3)\\right) \\left((1) + (3)\\right)} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right) \\\\ & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["2ca3c765-a8cc-5f28-93ee-3d5fd340c30b"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "071fc85e-b7ec-5343-9b00-518cdab61fb0" :answer/id #uuid "071fc85e-b7ec-5343-9b00-518cdab61fb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7430b7b6-9ff9-5f42-804a-ff990dfb7f5e" :answer/id #uuid "7430b7b6-9ff9-5f42-804a-ff990dfb7f5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "138" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "635b253f-5fcb-5ba4-9a33-1388e6f473f9" :answer/id #uuid "635b253f-5fcb-5ba4-9a33-1388e6f473f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "502b73fb-c85e-530b-b012-c7169375e747" :answer/id #uuid "502b73fb-c85e-530b-b012-c7169375e747" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "01282e04-9f20-5ce1-b4e5-ca694fd92ab4" :answer/id #uuid "01282e04-9f20-5ce1-b4e5-ca694fd92ab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-90" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "328fe164-3ff3-5e5e-b76d-41619193d616" :answer-field/id #uuid "328fe164-3ff3-5e5e-b76d-41619193d616" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["071fc85e-b7ec-5343-9b00-518cdab61fb0" "7430b7b6-9ff9-5f42-804a-ff990dfb7f5e" "635b253f-5fcb-5ba4-9a33-1388e6f473f9" "502b73fb-c85e-530b-b012-c7169375e747" "01282e04-9f20-5ce1-b4e5-ca694fd92ab4"] :answer-field/correct "071fc85e-b7ec-5343-9b00-518cdab61fb0" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "7b8c58a8-631b-5f56-81d9-dd2355b91a3c" :question/id #uuid "7b8c58a8-631b-5f56-81d9-dd2355b91a3c" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=\\left(\\left(3 x + 2 y\\right)^{2}\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\left(2 x + 3 y\\right)^{2}\\right)\\,j.$ \nEvaluate $\\nabla\\cdot F$ at the point $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=\\nabla\\cdot F=\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}.\n$$\n\nWhen differentiating $P$ with respect to $x$, hold $y$ constant; when differentiating $Q$ with respect to $y$, hold $x$ constant.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla\\cdot F & =\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(\\left(3 x + 2 y\\right)^{2})+\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(\\left(2 x + 3 y\\right)^{2}) \\\\  & =18 x + 12 y+\\left(12 x + 18 y\\right) \\\\  & =30 \\left(x + y\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(2,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\nabla\\cdot F)(2,1) & =30 (1) + 30 (2) \\\\ & =48+\\left(42\\right) \\\\ & =90.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["328fe164-3ff3-5e5e-b76d-41619193d616"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "303c1efb-11a4-5345-86f6-a486861e8209" :answer/id #uuid "303c1efb-11a4-5345-86f6-a486861e8209" :answer/type :answer.type/m